# ThermalControl Function Block (ST)

## Purpose
Controls heating stage of the tank cycle:
- Energizes heater until setpoint is reached.
- Signals completion when temperature achieved.

## Inputs
- `Cycle_Active : BOOL` — overall cycle running.
- `Mix_Complete : BOOL` — mixing finished.
- `Tn_Temp_Value : REAL` — current tank temperature.
- `Tn_Temp_Setpoint : REAL` — desired setpoint.

## Outputs
- `Heater : BOOL` — heater ON/OFF.
- `Heat_Complete : BOOL` — flag when heating done.

## Logic (ST)
```pascal
FUNCTION_BLOCK HeatManager_FB_ST
VAR_INPUT
    Cycle_Active     : BOOL;
    Mix_Complete     : BOOL;
    Tn_Temp_Value    : REAL;
    Tn_Temp_Setpoint : REAL;
END_VAR

VAR_OUTPUT
    Heater        : BOOL := FALSE;
    Heat_Complete : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR

IF Cycle_Active AND Mix_Complete THEN
    Heater := (Tn_Temp_Value < Tn_Temp_Setpoint);
    IF Tn_Temp_Value >= Tn_Temp_Setpoint THEN
        Heat_Complete := TRUE;
        Heater := FALSE;
    END_IF;
ELSE
    Heater := FALSE;
    Heat_Complete := FALSE;
END_IF;
